{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792232023,"nonce":"JwPktqOubcjzAFXksTozpDx7Zr8=","title":"The interpreter drops a closure's bound value when it is null, shifting every argument","message":"A closure that captures a null String (hasValue set, value null) was called without its bound first argument in the interpreter: five sites treated 'hasValue != 0 \u0026\u0026 value non-null' as bound. The callee's parameters then received the call's arguments one slot early. The old code appeared to work because the missing last parameter read as void and the program's answer happened not to depend on it; 8287782b's padding of omitted nullable arguments with null turned the shift into a Null access in interp and hybrid (--mode jit was unaffected).\n\nReproducer (chimpmonk-be): Lambda.exists(drafts, d -\u003e d.bone == remembered) with remembered:String = null raises 'Null access' in --mode interp/hybrid on main 272e12b4 and prints 'exists false' on main 6d6de12e. Fixture: crates/ash/test/tests/TestNullBoundClosure.hx (direct call, Lambda.exists/count/map, filter, null and non-null object captures).\n\nFix: a closure is bound when hasValue is set; a null value is passed as null. Stock HashLink calls fun(value, args...) whenever hasValue is set.","files":null}]}